{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality","id":1049285,"title":"Working From First Principles: Subjective Reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-15T07:24:47-08:00","id":1049285,"title":"Working From First Principles: Subjective Reality","content":"This sounds like a fun experiment. There's been a few mentions of Occam's Razor recently and it got me thinking: what happens when we start with a simple explanation and adjust it to cover objections.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to start with a single idea, listen to any objections as to why it doesn't work. Objections can be anything from logical incoherencies to violated themes to 'just doesn't feel right'. If I agree with the objection I will adjust the idea accordingly, if not, I'll explain why I think the current idea works. If it turns out I am making an assumption I didn't realize I was making I will add it to my approach. I won't accept all objections, but I'll try to address as many as possible. I have no idea what we will end up with but the journey should be fun.<br /> <br /> If you want to do the same thing (and I highly encourage this) state your overall approach and your core idea and let people start objecting. Everyone gets to be the judge of their own idea line but I encourage them to tackle even the things they don't like.<br /> <br /> <b>Approach: </b>I'm a big fan of the subjective reality side of Mage, and I like to avoid unchangeable things. I'm not particularly concerned with what the past actually looked like, but the modern world should look like the modern WoD and that includes historical evidence. Wherever possible I will choose solutions that rely on the Consensus, not on permanent cosmological constants. I reserve the right to duck objections involving time travel if they get too complicated. Above all, I want to keep that feeling of Reality on the Brink.<br /> <br /> <b>Ramnesis 1: </b>Reality is completely malleable. If you can get enough people to believe something it becomes true.<br /> <br /> If anyone does start with their own first principle I'll put it here.<br /> <br /> <b>Quantumboost 1:</b> The range of influence on Consensus increases with an entity's ability to reflect that range within itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Karlgust 1</b> - reality is TOTALLY subjective. What defines reality is the Consensus of all beings that reside within it. That encompass ALL beings - so, the majority of &quot;reality builders&quot; will be the spiritual beings. Therefore, humanity only play a small role in that dance. Furthermore, the beings don't all have the same role on that &quot;spiritual Consensus&quot;; greater beings have a greater role on that cosmic dance. The ideas and beliefs of Umbral lords and gods will have a far greater impact than that of a small semi intelligent spirit. However, reality is made by the shared beliefs/perceptions/thoughts of ALL beings, so, trillions of jagglings without real self awareness could have a bigger influence than a single incarnae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-16-2017, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T07:25:24-08:00","id":1049286,"title":"","content":"I'll make the first objection just to give you an idea of what I'm talking about. This is the one unchangeable element I knew we needed:<br /> <br /> <b>Objection to Ramnesis 1</b>: If people don't believe reality is Consensual, wouldn't they take away their ability to change it? What about when a society thinks some people aren't people? Wouldn't the non-people no longer affect the consensus?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's a contradiction. Two in fact. Paradoxically, for reality to be consensual, the Consensus itself has to be objectively true be. So:<br /> <br /> <b>Ramnesis 2:</b> Reality is almost completely malleable. If you can get enough people to believe something it becomes true. The Conensus cannot change who affects it or change anyone's personhood. <br /> <br /> Now I know for a fact that this doesn't fit Mage as we know it, but I want to hear objections other than my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:00:07-08:00","id":1049318,"title":"","content":"Objection might a strong word, but I'll keep with the formatting anyway:<br /> <br /> <b>Objection to Approach</b>: &quot;Consensual&quot; is not thoroughly defined. How much weight does a group of believers need to have to alter Reality? Plurality, majority, near unanimity (if so by what degree), unanimous? If Consensus is dictated by plurality or majority, what happens to almost won beliefs (ex: 51% vs 49% of believers in conflict with each other distributed evenly to discount for Reality Zone formation)? Who is a &quot;person&quot; in regards to defining Consensus, and are &quot;persons&quot; equal? Do persons impact the Consensual Reality even if they lack capacity to have a belief in something (examples: Can a newborn infant impact the value of delayed gratification? Can person that has always been blind impact what blue looks like?). Do persons have &quot;range&quot; of belief (aka do my beliefs weaken their impact on Consensus the farther away I am from an event)?<br /> <br /> <b>Objection to Ramnesis 2</b>: In accordance with the need for the modern world to exist as it does on a superficial level, the anthropic principle must be in play on some level (that is the rules of the universe must both allow for the current state of the world to exist, and the rules must have played out in a fashion that lead to the current state), isn't there a requirement that somehow a &quot;person&quot; or group of &quot;persons&quot; defined reality so strongly that certain aspects of reality are nearly immutable on the large scale? While somewhat contingent on the above questions, as a example, if a spiritual entity of sufficient power called Gaia both counts as a person for Consensus and has an unequal impact on Consensus to the point where humanity as a whole cannot override Gaia, could Gaia be empowering rules that are effectively constant (perhaps even to the point where every other person believes in them for being seemingly constant and would persist even after Gaia ceased to)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:51:53-08:00","id":1049370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049318#post1049318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objection might a strong word, but I'll keep with the formatting anyway:<br /> <br /> <b>Objection to Approach</b>: &quot;Consensual&quot; is not thoroughly defined. How much weight does a group of believers need to have to alter Reality? Plurality, majority, near unanimity (if so by what degree), unanimous? If Consensus is dictated by plurality or majority, what happens to almost won beliefs (ex: 51% vs 49% of believers in conflict with each other distributed evenly to discount for Reality Zone formation)? Who is a &quot;person&quot; in regards to defining Consensus, and are &quot;persons&quot; equal? Do persons impact the Consensual Reality even if they lack capacity to have a belief in something (examples: Can a newborn infant impact the value of delayed gratification? Can person that has always been blind impact what blue looks like?). Do persons have &quot;range&quot; of belief (aka do my beliefs weaken their impact on Consensus the farther away I am from an event)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to call this an objection to the idea. The approach is more so you have an idea which way I am going to lean.<br /> <br /> And yeah, that's a good objection. I'd ordinarily hesitate to give specific numerical thresholds, but hell let's see if it works. Lets go with 10% is the bare minimum for something to happen, 66% makes it likely, 80% makes it certain. Also yes on the range, but I'm going to duck any specific numbers because that math is more complicated.<br /> <br /> On the subject of personhood, I'm going to refrain from limiting it at this point as I don't want to limit anything if I don't have to. Specifying local belief might handle any problems that come from supernatural input anyways. I do think that everyone affecting the consensus equally is technically implicit in the wording so that doesn't need to be changed (although I admit I'm stretching on that one) I also think that while babies do count, they don't have any beliefs and so don't affect the consensus in any positive or negative way. No need for a change there either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Objection to Ramnesis 2</b>: In accordance with the need for the modern world to exist as it does on a superficial level, the anthropic principle must be in play on some level (that is the rules of the universe must both allow for the current state of the world to exist, and the rules must have played out in a fashion that lead to the current state), isn't there a requirement that somehow a &quot;person&quot; or group of &quot;persons&quot; defined reality so strongly that certain aspects of reality are nearly immutable on the large scale? While somewhat contingent on the above questions, as a example, if a spiritual entity of sufficient power called Gaia both counts as a person for Consensus and has an unequal impact on Consensus to the point where humanity as a whole cannot override Gaia, could Gaia be empowering rules that are effectively constant (perhaps even to the point where every other person believes in them for being seemingly constant and would persist even after Gaia ceased to)? </div> </div> </div>Tricky. It's a distinct possibility, but one I'm trying to avoid so I'd like to try to reason around it if I can. Can I get some specific of elements that should be immutable?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> For now, let's go with:<br /> <br /> <b>Ramnesis 3</b>: Reality is almost completely malleable. If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, 80% and it's certain. The Conensus cannot change who affects it or change anyone's personhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:50:30-08:00","id":1049400,"title":"","content":"The problem is that spirits are 'persons' by the definitions of cWoD and, since spirits outnumber human beings by orders of magnitude, the beliefs of spirits would have more weight than the beliefs of humans. While human belief might effect whether or not True Magick is coincidental or vulgar, the beliefs of spirits would basically prevent human beliefs from changing the foundations of reality even within a Consensual Reality model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T11:59:31-08:00","id":1049405,"title":"","content":"The premise demands two things:<br /> 1. Existence of humans at the very start.<br /> 2. Protected status of humanity as the class of superbeings that warp reality.<br /> <br /> This further creates problems such as &quot;what is human&quot; and &quot;what is personhood&quot;.<br /> <br /> The simplest objection I can offer is a moral one. Jews really were behind the decline of Germany. Gay people, crossgender people and other 'freaks' really are possessed by demons. Foreigners really did ruin America. Black people deserved it because they didn't believe hard enough.<br /> The other objection I can offer is that the setting built on the premise of subjective reality is unusable. Not for urban fantasy anyway. I can't even imagine what contrivances you'd have to pull to make a subjective reality setting to look like our objective reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:01:11-08:00","id":1049407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049400#post1049400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that spirits are 'persons' by the definitions of cWoD</div> </div> </div> </div>What definitions would those be? Humans in cWoD have a soul and spirits don't. Humans were created by YHVH and spirits are just an unfortunate side effect of fallen angles messing with the Lore of Realms. That already makes humans and spirits different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T12:48:43-08:00","id":1049436,"title":"","content":"<b>Objection to Ramnesis 3:</b> If 80% believe something (unrelated to personhood or meta-Consensus etc.), but 10% believe in something which contradicts that, and 'enough' believe in the contradictory nature of those two possibilities, then you would have the lesser-believed thing be 'possible', but the greater-believed thing being 'certain' rather than uncertain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T13:36:51-08:00","id":1049451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049370#post1049370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd ordinarily hesitate to give specific numerical thresholds, but hell let's see if it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the example numbers are an interesting idea, I think there's more important issue in the fundamental nature of how Consensus works. It very hard to reasonably expand on the base explanation of how a subjective reality works if the main mechanism of how reality is affected by subjectivity isn't thoroughly defined.<br /> <br /> This specific thing also has issues as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6072_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6072\" data-vbnamecard=\"6072\">Quantumboost</a> already hit on, were you can have conflicting beliefs in the same area without any clear idea of what this makes Reality look like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do think that everyone affecting the consensus equally is technically implicit in the wording so that doesn't need to be changed (although I admit I'm stretching on that one) I also think that while babies do count, they don't have any beliefs and so don't affect the consensus in any positive or negative way. No need for a change there either. </div> </div> </div>I'd disagree with the the assumption that consensus implies equality. If two parents and three children reach a consensus on where to go out for dinner, it doesn't mean that everyone actually has equal power in the decision making process. The parents in particularly have the ability to effectively veto any choice the children make even if they are outnumbered.<br /> <br /> Babies do have rudimentary beliefs, even if they're extremely superficial ones shaped by their environment to the point where they probably can't impact anything. But this doesn't address the blind man's influence on the Reality of visual appearance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tricky. It's a distinct possibility, but one I'm trying to avoid so I'd like to try to reason around it if I can. </div> </div> </div>The Gaia solution is an example of many possible iterations of the same concept of a progenitor person that creates a stable enough reality for the current state of Reality to manifest itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I get some specific of elements that should be immutable? </div> </div> </div>Well, this doesn't assume anything is truly immutable, just effectively immutable due to metaphysical inertia. <br /> <br /> A lot of these though would be the rough natural laws that mirror our objective reality: gravity, basic properties of matter, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049405#post1049405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise demands two things:<br /> 1. Existence of humans at the very start.<br /> 2. Protected status of humanity as the class of superbeings that warp reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. The premise does not inherently suppose the humans are the only beings that can participate in Consensus. And if anything, not demanding these things by not restraining it to humans makes a stable reality that emerges out of the pure chaos of pre-Consensus reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049407#post1049407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What definitions would those be? Humans in cWoD have a soul and spirits don't. Humans were created by YHVH and spirits are just an unfortunate side effect of fallen angles messing with the Lore of Realms. That already makes humans and spirits different.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Mage makes it clear that the Avatar (which is what makes human special in regards to Consensus), which is not the same thing as a soul (varied on how one defines a soul) even if they are metaphysically linked.<br /> <br /> 2) The WOD does not posit that Demon's metaphysics are the absolute truth of the setting.<br /> <br /> 3) Some spirits and related entities are clearly capable of defining reality at least on a local level. Paradox spirits, Avatars, Psychopomp spirits, as well as spirits in Umbral Realms that are shaped without the influence of humans all canonically exist. Even if not all spirits participate in Consensus, some clearly do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:29:41-08:00","id":1049493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049318#post1049318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do persons have &quot;range&quot; of belief (aka do my beliefs weaken their impact on Consensus the farther away I am from an event)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's not a matter of space distance (space is... An illusion of the Consensus perhaps?), but rather a matter of <i>connection</i>... Metaphysic connection between events. Just like the correspondence table","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:34:31-08:00","id":1049499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049451#post1049451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Some spirits and related entities are clearly capable of defining reality at least on a local level. Paradox spirits, Avatars, Psychopomp spirits, as well as spirits in Umbral Realms that are shaped without the influence of humans all canonically exist. Even if not all spirits participate in Consensus, some clearly do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building off that, it's entirely plausible that the 'weight' of influence on Consensus is based on how powerful+complex+aware a being is. Power means that enough 'stuff' is tied to the contributor that they basically count as multiples by sheer bulk. Complex means that its self-image encompasses more detail and reality. Aware means that it can observe the world and contribute to Consensus about not-itself.<br /> <br /> Maybe everything <i>is</i> a contributor to Consensus, and only things that possess beyond a certain level of awareness can extend that beyond 'mere' ontological inertia to something other than 'being itself'. Humans might get to 'cheat' by naturally being things that create representations of other things within themselves, letting them influence Consensus related to other things noticeably without first being Celestine-grade; meanwhile, maybe spirits don't do so before that level because they're too... self-centered, I guess.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, gonna propose some of that as another &quot;first principle&quot;:<br /> <b>Quantumboost 1:</b> The range of influence on Consensus increases with an entity's ability to reflect that range within itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 02-15-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T14:37:41-08:00","id":1049502,"title":"","content":"Heck, if you assume that the belief of spirits are capable of shaping reality, then the differences between Objective Reality and Subjective Reality are academic. Just out of curiosity, where does it say in Mage that the sleeping Avatar is the mechanism by which human belief shapes the Consensus? And Jagglings are presented as being as sapient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-15-2017, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:11:25-08:00","id":1049519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049318#post1049318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Objection to Ramnesis 2</b>: In accordance with the need for the modern world to exist as it does on a superficial level, the anthropic principle must be in play on some level (that is the rules of the universe must both allow for the current state of the world to exist, and the rules must have played out in a fashion that lead to the current state), isn't there a requirement that somehow a &amp;quot;person&amp;quot; or group of &amp;quot;persons&amp;quot; defined reality so strongly that certain aspects of reality are nearly immutable on the large scale? While somewhat contingent on the above questions, as a example, if a spiritual entity of sufficient power called Gaia both counts as a person for Consensus and has an unequal impact on Consensus to the point where humanity as a whole cannot override Gaia, could Gaia be empowering rules that are effectively constant (perhaps even to the point where every other person believes in them for being seemingly constant and would persist even after Gaia ceased to)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my own personal theory. Consensus is everything. But humanity ISN'T the only source of Consensus - actually, it aint even the greatest source of it.<br /> <br /> In my theory, all &quot;entities&quot; out there are responsible for the Universal Consensus... That means all plants, animals, vampires, werewolves, centaurs, whatever.<br /> <br /> But it also means that the biggest source of Consensus are the umbrals. The spirits.<br /> <br /> I also think that all beings AREN'T equal contributors to the universal Consensus. It could be debatable if a cosmic entity like the Wyrm or the Weaver or even Gaia could be a sentient being (or just a natural force like gravity), but those higher beings would be &quot;bigger contributors&quot; to the &quot;universal Consensus&quot; than a fly. <br /> <br /> So, we could say, for example, that ENTROPY, the process o decay of all the creation, only exists because those are THE WYRM'S (ENTITY) THOUGHTS. Basically, the entity the Garou call &quot;Wyrm&quot; think about death, destruction and decay... And it's thoughts are reflected upon the reality.<br /> <br /> The Weaver entity thinks about ecstasy... And it brings pattern about the world.<br /> <br /> The One thinks about the Tellurian... And so, the Universe IS.<br /> <br /> Lesser beings contribute to this cosmic song too:<br /> <br /> The Sun celestine, if you like that idea of antropoformization of everything from WtA, and do consider the Sun a sentient entity, you could have the Sun (entity) thoughts be about heat, light, energy. That would be the reason of why the Sun heats the Earth: that's the contribution of the Sun entity to universal Consensus.<br /> <br /> Even lesser beings keep contributing by lesser degrees. So, dirty have this brown aparence, the texture that soil has, because of the millions, millions, trillions or gazillions of earth elementals that as a whole determine the Consensus about earth, rocks, soil, dirty. That's too are were you'll see the differences: maybe one group of earth elementals close to a court of water elementals, started thinking about clay, while another group that became friends with fire elementals, developed thoughts about vulcanic rocks. That's why you would have different kinds of soil, earth, dirty etc - &quot;different earthly Consensus&quot;... Something we could call of &quot;divergente of opinions&quot; that earth elementals may have about their &quot;universes&quot; (I think that rocks and soil would encompass the entire universe of earth elementals).<br /> <br /> Rivers are made by water elementals that agree amoungst each other that salt is an abhorent substance. All River elementals agree that &quot;saltless&quot; should be the &quot;water Consensus&quot;. Of course, ocean elementals think the idea of saltless water not only ridiculous or heretic, but insane... In fact, they probably can't even conceive of the notion of water without salt. The Consensus of &quot;salt water&quot; is a belief strongly held by ALL oceanic water elementals.<br /> <br /> And so forth.<br /> <br /> Most spirits are bound by their roles; so, they are both the creators of Consensus just as much as a product of it.<br /> <br /> In time they could change, and become new things... That's how an earth elemental and a water elemental can get too close toghether, start &quot;comparing notes&quot; (in a metaphysical non literal way) and give birth to &quot;mud elementals&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T15:33:11-08:00","id":1049529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality#post1049285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ramnesis 1: </b>Reality is completely malleable. If you can get enough people to believe something it becomes true.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Scenario given R1: </b>Suppose the critical number of people were persuaded to believe that reality was not completely malleable. Would reality adapt to this belief?<br /> <b>If Yes: </b>If reality ceased being malleable, then it could not be changed later and this R1 would not be true any longer. Thus later reversions to the belief that reality was malleable would not change reality back to being malleable, since the initial changed belief would be for an unmalleable reality. Reality cannot be made completely unmalleable, therefore it is not completely malleable, and thus R1 is not true.<br /> <b>If No:</b> Then R1 is not true.<br /> <br /> \u2234 R1 cannot be true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 02-15-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:12:49-08:00","id":1049591,"title":"","content":"An interesting point built on a valid logical paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:25:03-08:00","id":1049598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049400#post1049400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that spirits are 'persons' by the definitions of cWoD and, since spirits outnumber human beings by orders of magnitude, the beliefs of spirits would have more weight than the beliefs of humans. While human belief might effect whether or not True Magick is coincidental or vulgar, the beliefs of spirits would basically prevent human beliefs from changing the foundations of reality even within a Consensual Reality model.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's exactly my personal view on what &quot;Reality Foundations&quot; truly are.<br /> <br /> In fact, I've been wanting to place that entire idea on the topic about &quot;1001 paradigms&quot; or something like it... I call it the &quot;Scientific Animism&quot; Paradigm, a paradigm for techno-shamans mostly. Gravity works, plants use the sunlight to produce sugar and light is the faster thing there is. The catch: photon spirits &quot;believe&quot; light to travel at 300 thousands kilometers per second, water elementals &quot;believe&quot; that they turn to gas at 100 Celsius, and so on.<br /> <br /> Same world, same mechanics... Different principles. All of the suddenly, gravity is no longer a natural law, but the will of gazillions of extra dimensional beings that &quot;believe&quot; it away.<br /> <br /> Entropy? The Wyrm thought it away (or that force is created by the &quot;spiritual Consensus&quot; of gazillions of banes)<br /> <br /> Pattern? Gazillions of pattern spiders &quot;Consensus it&quot; away. Or, the Weaver entity do it. Or perhaps, it's the sum of Weaver (holding the biggest pull on the &quot;Pattern Consensus&quot;) plus all Patter/Weaver spirits, working toghether to &quot;believe&quot; the &quot;Pattern Consensus&quot;.<br /> <br /> So... Is the thoughts of the Wyrm that create the universe's entropy?<br /> <br /> It's possible. Well, in that case, it could be possible to ERRADICATE the Entropy... If you could &quot;convince&quot; the Wyrm to not want to destroy things. It could be that &quot;simple&quot; actually.<br /> <br /> Or, you could end gravity if you can convince trillions of gravitons spirits that their idea of pulling everything is stupid... Convince a gazillion of gravity gafflings, and gravity will be no more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:31:30-08:00","id":1049606,"title":"","content":"Which is fine, it does not really matter to me if objective reality is constructed by Celestine-level spirits or physical laws. As long as neither plays favorites among everyday people, I am satisfied with the results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T17:47:26-08:00","id":1049616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049502#post1049502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, if you assume that the belief of spirits are capable of shaping reality, then the differences between Objective Reality and Subjective Reality are academic. Just out of curiosity, where does it say in Mage that the sleeping Avatar is the mechanism by which human belief shapes the Consensus? And Jagglings are presented as being as sapient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I agree, that's ALMOST an academic issue, in my opnion. So, here it goes:<br /> <br /> <b>Karlgust 1</b> - reality is TOTALLY subjective. What defines reality is the Consensus of all beings that reside within it. That encompass ALL beings - so, the majority of &quot;reality builders&quot; will be the spiritual beings. Therefore, humanity only play a small role in that dance. Furthermore, the beings don't all have the same role on that &quot;spiritual Consensus&quot;; greater beings have a greater role on that cosmic dance. The ideas and beliefs of Umbral lords and gods will have a far greater impact than that of a small semi intelligent spirit. However, reality is made by the shared beliefs/perceptions/thoughts of ALL beings, so, trillions of jagglings without real self awareness could have a bigger influence than a single incarnae.<br /> <br /> In that dance, humanity can also influence, but it aint big enough to dictate all the rules.<br /> <br /> So... My Paradigm is... The world is written under scientific principles. But those principles are kept by animistic will. So... Science IS animistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T19:19:20-08:00","id":1049654,"title":"","content":"Some evidences for this &quot;Spiritual Consensus&quot;: the Wyrm/Weaver change.<br /> <br /> If you like the WtA lore (which I, personally, don't like to include in my Mage games), the Weaver were happy about creating patterns for things and the Wyrm were happy keeping the tellurian balanced.<br /> <br /> But the Weaver <i>changed it's way of thinking </i>. So, it imprisoned the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> That, as a consequence, changed the &quot;Wyrm Consensus&quot;. No longer believing in keeping the balance in the creation, the Wyrm became insane, and sought the destruction of the world.<br /> <br /> That change in the Wyrm's Paradigm actually changed the Consensus about Entropy... Entropy would no longer be a force that keep things balanced, but would rather become a source of destruction and corruption. <br /> <br /> That's a huge change on &quot;Consensus&quot; thanks to the changes in the worldviews of a single entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:51:55-08:00","id":1049825,"title":"","content":"Brace yourselves, this is going to be a long one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049400#post1049400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that spirits are 'persons' by the definitions of cWoD and, since spirits outnumber human beings by orders of magnitude, the beliefs of spirits would have more weight than the beliefs of humans. While human belief might effect whether or not True Magick is coincidental or vulgar, the beliefs of spirits would basically prevent human beliefs from changing the foundations of reality even within a Consensual Reality model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm pretty sure I'm going to have to revise the idea to cover this, but let's see how far we can get before we do.<br /> <br /> I think there's an interesting dynamic going on between the nature of spirits and the 'local' consensus, because what is local to them is the Umbra and they do have a lot of influence over what form it takes. So from a certain point of view that could be the effect of their impact on the consensus.<br /> <br /> In fact, given the effect the Umbra has on the physical world and vice versa, that could even serve as a stabilizing effect that keeps things from changing too quickly.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Mage 2nd strongly implied that spirits did contribute to the consensus, though later books backed off that claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049405#post1049405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest objection I can offer is a moral one. Jews really were behind the decline of Germany. Gay people, crossgender people and other 'freaks' really are possessed by demons. Foreigners really did ruin America. Black people deserved it because they didn't believe hard enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one thing I was trying to head off by saying the consensus couldn't alter itself or remove someone's personhood. Obviously it wasn't enough. How about<b></b>: <i>The Consensus cannot change who affects it, change anyone's personhood, or change their mental or spiritual state.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other objection I can offer is that the setting built on the premise of subjective reality is unusable. Not for urban fantasy anyway. I can't even imagine what contrivances you'd have to pull to make a subjective reality setting to look like our objective reality. </div> </div> </div>That's one thing I'm hoping to find out with this experiment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049436#post1049436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Objection to Ramnesis 3:</b> If 80% believe something (unrelated to personhood or meta-Consensus etc.), but 10% believe in something which contradicts that, and 'enough' believe in the contradictory nature of those two possibilities, then you would have the lesser-believed thing be 'possible', but the greater-believed thing being 'certain' rather than uncertain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in a quandry on this one because that's a clear contradiction, but on the other hand, Reality on the Brink. So I probably should revise the idea but I really want to just live with the Paradox if I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049451#post1049451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd disagree with the the assumption that consensus implies equality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually referring to the words &quot;enough people&quot; since that implies it is numerical rather than qualitative advantage. I also realize I was needlessly ducking the issue, so I'm going to formalize this and see where it takes us. <i>Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Babies do have rudimentary beliefs, even if they're extremely superficial ones shaped by their environment to the point where they probably can't impact anything. But this doesn't address the blind man's influence on the Reality of visual appearance. </div> </div> </div>No, you are right, it doesn't, at least not in all cases. The threshold numbers might, though. Are there enough blind people who believe strange things about appearance to push the modern world away from what we expect it to be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gaia solution is an example of many possible iterations of the same concept of a progenitor person that creates a stable enough reality for the current state of Reality to manifest itself. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, this doesn't assume anything is truly immutable, just effectively immutable due to metaphysical inertia.<br /> A lot of these though would be the rough natural laws that mirror our objective reality: gravity, basic properties of matter, etc. </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Let me split this into two separate problems. (1) Starting Conditions - If you start at some arbitrary world, say immaterial people floating in a void and absorbing raw ether, can you get to a world of gravity, physical interaction, and three dimensional space? (2) Metaphysical Inertia - Once you have a world of gravity, physical interaction, and three dimensional space, can it maintain itself (over a long time frame) without outside help?<br /> <br /> For (2) I don't think we need a Metaphysical Inertia because the Inertia of Expectation will handle things. Gravity, motion, space, and air are all things we start learning on day one. Before we even have language we have deep expectations about how certain things work. They should resist change already due to how deep and universal they are.<br /> But that same argument makes (1) difficult. I could imagine a slow evolution between worlds, but it would take a <i>long</i> time and many thousands of generations. Explaining new phenomena and new limitations would also be tricky.<br /> <br /> Although, a shift from two dimensions to three could easily result in a gravity like force with reasoning like 'there was always a third dimension, there was just some force that kept us from moving that direction.' So the potential is there.<br /> <br /> Still, it is worth saying that <i>at some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating.</i><br /> <br /> So:<br /> <b>Ramnesis 4</b>: Reality is almost completely malleable. If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, 80% and it's certain. <i>Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating.</i> The Conensus cannot change who affects it or change anyone's personhood, <i>or change their mental or spiritual state.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049529#post1049529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Scenario given R1: </b>Suppose the critical number of people were persuaded to believe that reality was not completely malleable. Would reality adapt to this belief?<br /> <b>If Yes: </b>If reality ceased being malleable, then it could not be changed later and this R1 would not be true any longer. Thus later reversions to the belief that reality was malleable would not change reality back to being malleable, since the initial changed belief would be for an unmalleable reality. Reality cannot be made completely unmalleable, therefore it is not completely malleable, and thus R1 is not true.<br /> <b>If No:</b> Then R1 is not true.<br /> <br /> \u2234 R1 cannot be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Ramnesis 2, 3, and 4 cover this problem to your satisfaction?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:08:04-08:00","id":1049831,"title":"","content":"But then it is not a subjective reality, it is an objective reality with high levels of plasticity. And, anyway, the Consensus can influence spirits, so how does that work with the unchanging nature of personhood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:55:39-08:00","id":1049846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049831#post1049831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then it is not a subjective reality, it is an objective reality with high levels of plasticity. And, anyway, the Consensus can influence spirits, so how does that work with the unchanging nature of personhood?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is still subjective. Wipe out all the spirits and reality changes according to the new Consensus.<br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't say the Consensus changes spirits, I'd say it changes reality and Spirits adjust to reflect. If the Consensus changes the world so that it is always cold, that will drastically change humanity's outlook, but that's a secondary effect. The Consensus didn't force people to change their mind, it just set up a situation where they would of their own accord.<br /> <br /> I do think you are homing in on a contradiction here, something feels wrong about what I just said, but I don't know what it is yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:55:58-08:00","id":1049847,"title":"","content":"Can it? It could be that the Consensus provides different masks. Simply a change in perception not a change of the spirit proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:57:43-08:00","id":1049848,"title":"","content":"What created the Consensus though? If it predates humanity, it is really a Consensus or just flexible natural laws?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:42:31-08:00","id":1049874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049848#post1049848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What created the Consensus though? If it predates humanity, it is really a Consensus or just flexible natural laws?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the consensus is a giant mindless spirit that is impossible to detect. Anything that shapes the consensus is within the spirits control, anything that doesn't, isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T10:43:55-08:00","id":1049926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049499#post1049499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Quantumboost 1:</b> The range of influence on Consensus increases with an entity's ability to reflect that range within itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Objection to Quantumboost 1:</b> There's a potential chain reaction here. If a being (say an Umbral representation of an omnipotent god) is believed to be more connected to things it will become so. As it does it's own ability to reflect things will grow. With no natural limit, one creature (or a few) could grow to massively dominate reality to the point that no one else gets a say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049616#post1049616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Karlgust 1</b> - reality is TOTALLY subjective. What defines reality is the Consensus of all beings that reside within it. That encompass ALL beings - so, the majority of &quot;reality builders&quot; will be the spiritual beings. Therefore, humanity only play a small role in that dance. Furthermore, the beings don't all have the same role on that &quot;spiritual Consensus&quot;; greater beings have a greater role on that cosmic dance. The ideas and beliefs of Umbral lords and gods will have a far greater impact than that of a small semi intelligent spirit. However, reality is made by the shared beliefs/perceptions/thoughts of ALL beings, so, trillions of jagglings without real self awareness could have a bigger influence than a single incarnae.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Objection to Karlgust 1:</b> Two objections actually.<br /> <br /> 1) There are a potentially infinite number of creatures out past the far horizons. Why don't their alien beliefs completely invalidate our local influences.<br /> <br /> 2) If this were true the Technocracy would spend most of their efforts manipulating and assassinating umbral beings and care very little about the actions of Reality Deviants? That sounds like a significant change in focus.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, the Nephandi's actions make a hell of a lot more sense this way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:31:15-08:00","id":1049959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049825#post1049825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Ramnesis 2, 3, and 4 cover this problem to your satisfaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not especially, because my scenario was meant to examine what would happen if people adapted an affirmative belief about the nature of subjective reality. If reality is subjective, can it be made not-subjective by sufficient belief? <br /> <br /> <b>Scenario 2</b>: A sufficient number of people to alter consensual reality believe in Des Moines, Iowa's Civic Center there exists a representation of a square circle. They do not believe any special definitions of the terms 'square' or 'circle', and believe that a square is a regular two-dimensional geometric shape with exactly four sides of equal length, and that a circle is a regular two-dimensional geometric shape with exactly one side, each point of which is equidistant from the midpoint of a line segment that bisects the shape.<br /> <br /> What do we see in the Des Moines Civic Center when we go to see the thing that is believed to exist?<br /> <br /> <b>Purpose of the Scenario</b>: Does the nature of consensual reality permit the existence of a thing with mutually exclusive attributes? A logical impossibility, if you would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:14:57-08:00","id":1049979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049825#post1049825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, Mage 2nd strongly implied that spirits did contribute to the consensus, though later books backed off that claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised came back pretty hard to this once it got into more spirit stuff after avoiding it due to the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm in a quandry on this one because that's a clear contradiction, but on the other hand, Reality on the Brink. So I probably should revise the idea but I really want to just live with the Paradox if I can. </div> </div> </div>I think addressing this has to go back to a more thorough definition of Consensus. I'm aware you have good reasons to try to minimize the focus on that, but it really feels like you can't escape the necessity to get into more detail about to maintain a coherent evolution from the first principle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there enough blind people who believe strange things about appearance to push the modern world away from what we expect it to be? </div> </div> </div>On a broad scale? No. On a local Reality Zone scale? There are places where this could be an issue. For example there's an island in the pacific where all the current inhabitants are descended from a shipwreck's survivors. With a low genetic diversity and founder effect in play, a rare genetic eye condition (which results in a strange form of color-blindness and high levels of light sensitivity) is extremely common in this one place. So until that island reconnected with the modern world, it would have to be the case that on that island things looked fundamentally different than the same version of those things elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (1) Starting Conditions - If you start at some arbitrary world, say immaterial people floating in a void and absorbing raw ether, can you get to a world of gravity, physical interaction, and three dimensional space? </div> </div> </div>Why not? At that point reality is so mutable that as long as the number of people in it is small enough, they could create whatever they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (2) Metaphysical Inertia - Once you have a world of gravity, physical interaction, and three dimensional space, can it maintain itself (over a long time frame) without outside help?<br /> <br /> For (2) I don't think we need a Metaphysical Inertia because the Inertia of Expectation will handle things. </div> </div> </div>Given the premise of a subjective reality I'm uncertain as to the difference between Metaphysical Inertia and Expectation Inertia. Expectations only have inertia in this context because of the metaphysics involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that same argument makes (1) difficult. I could imagine a slow evolution between worlds, but it would take a <i>long</i> time and many thousands of generations. Explaining new phenomena and new limitations would also be tricky. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why I started with the Gaia example of one person defining a world that is then populated by lots of persons that have never known the raw subjectivity of the first person and thus generate the inertia of these principles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ramnesis 4</b>: Reality is almost completely malleable. If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, 80% and it's certain. <i>Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating.</i> The Conensus cannot change who affects it or change anyone's personhood, <i>or change their mental or spiritual state.</i> </div> </div> </div><b>Objection to Ramnesis 4</b>: How does equal potential impact on Consensus logically flow with unequal strength of individual beliefs? If equality of impact is a fundamental aspect of Consensus, then beliefs can only be as strong as the weight of belief in them. There's no mechanism for a belief to gain strength in excess of net balance of extant beliefs by all applicable persons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do Ramnesis 2, 3, and 4 cover this problem to your satisfaction? </div> </div> </div>I think this is another issue that's less with the growing principle, and more like my initial &quot;objection to approach.&quot; There's an axiomatic issue with the ill-defined nature of Consensus. That is, Consensus is an axiom of this experiment without the direct definition an axiom should have. Too an extent, we're trying to do algebra where &quot;addition/subtraction,&quot; is not well defined. Even if there's some algebra you can do without defining addition/subtraction, it gets very limited and creates an incomplete set of principles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:17:54-08:00","id":1049983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049959#post1049959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not especially, because my scenario was meant to examine what would happen if people adapted an affirmative belief about the nature of subjective reality. If reality is subjective, can it be made not-subjective by sufficient belief?<br /> <br /> Ah, preventing that specific contradiction was the purpose of Ramnesis 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Scenario 2</b>: A sufficient number of people to alter consensual reality believe in Des Moines, Iowa's Civic Center there exists a representation of a square circle. They do not believe any special definitions of the terms 'square' or 'circle', and believe that a square is a regular two-dimensional geometric shape with exactly four sides of equal length, and that a circle is a regular two-dimensional geometric shape with exactly one side, each point of which is equidistant from the midpoint of a line segment that bisects the shape.<br /> <br /> What do we see in the Des Moines Civic Center when we go to see the thing that is believed to exist?<br /> <br /> <b>Purpose of the Scenario</b>: Does the nature of consensual reality permit the existence of a thing with mutually exclusive attributes? A logical impossibility, if you would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think. I think the problem here is that we the onlookers don't have a clue what the people are actually expecting to see when they look at this thing. The difficulty seems to be coming from our own lack of imagination. If we chose a more familiar situation, such as the dress is both white and blue or the cat is both alive and dead, we get something that is still a contradiction, but one we are more familiar with. The dress, in particular, might be a good example of how that kind of contradiction would play out when exposed to scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:29:18-08:00","id":1049994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049926#post1049926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Objection to Karlgust 1:</b> Two objections actually.<br /> <br /> 1) There are a potentially infinite number of creatures out past the far horizons. Why don't their alien beliefs completely invalidate our local influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn Malfeans above the Oblivion, along with all the Onceborn malfeans and probably some millions of specters make the Labirinth into the absolutely alien landscape that it is. The closer you are to those beings, the greater the impact of their &quot;Consensus&quot;. Further away from that, you'll have the Tempest, also a alien landscape, but not as unforgiven as the Labirinth, the level of influence of the specters is somewhat lesser. And above that, you'll have the Shadownlands, which will have a lot more influence from wraiths than specters.<br /> <br /> The Low Umbra, however, is totally alien. And, the further away from the material world and deeper in itself you move, the more alien it is - and the more it ressembles its own alien residents.<br /> <br /> If you go inside the Dreaming... Just the same. That's a place with it's own laws, and the further away from our reality, the less those laws ressembles ours.<br /> <br /> The High Umbra also is absolutely alien. Once again, the further away from us, the more the local laws are unlike Earth.<br /> <br /> In fact, I would say that this aspect of, lets call it &quot;local spirit Consensus&quot;, it anything I believe it gives a BIGGER cause for this idea which we could call &quot;The One Consensus theory&quot; or &quot;Gaian Consensus theory&quot;. Why?<br /> <br /> Take the Abyss in the Middle Umbra. Why does this realm have so many very specific laws built into it?<br /> <br /> You see, everybody say &quot;oh, the reality of WoD is objective... You have a series of laws that are set in Stone, they are fundamental Foundations&quot;... But that's simply NOT TRUE.<br /> <br /> The Oblivion for instance, defies all the mass and energy conservation laws of the material world... Specters (un)luck enough to be sucked away by it are GONE. The Oblivion is a Void of nothingness, so all that it sucks away, cease to be entirely. Oblivion actually makes &quot;spiritual mass&quot; disappear from the Tapestry.<br /> <br /> A place like the Dreaming, or the Digital Web, defies almost all laws of the material world. That includes even laws about space and time, which are perhaps amongst the most basic building blocks of the material reality.<br /> <br /> And the Deep Umbra could be said to be an ANTI reality.<br /> <br /> But, if we say that &quot;Consensus is everything, and all beings are responsible for building it, including spirits&quot;, all those troubles are solved. Neverborn, onceborn and millions of specters (plus a gazillion of plasmics) are the ones that make the labirinth what it is. Chimeras are the responsibles for the Dreaming. And things-men-were-not-meant-to-know makes the Deep Umbra so alien.<br /> <br /> Why don't the aliens of the Deep Umbra change the material world into the negative zone?<br /> <br /> Well... They try.<br /> <br /> But they are not the only ones responsible for Consensus right?<br /> <br /> In fact, that idea also plays well for all the spiritual barriers of the realities.<br /> <br /> Realities with local Consensus too different will have a strong &quot;Paradigm Wall&quot;, lets call it.<br /> <br /> Thats essentially what the Gauntlet is. <br /> <br /> Even more so, the &quot; Dream Shell&quot;, the barrier that keeps the Deep Umbra away, would be the barrier were the alien &quot;Cthulhu Consensus&quot; simply can't mix with the rest of &quot;Umbral Consensus&quot;.<br /> <br /> All those ideas actually play incredibly well with a concept like &quot;reality zones&quot;. Basically, every Realm on every Umbra would be a kind of a different &quot;spiritual reality zone&quot;, where local &quot;spiritual Consensus&quot; has enough specifics to generate a segregated reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049926#post1049926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If this were true the Technocracy would spend most of their efforts manipulating and assassinating umbral beings and care very little about the actions of Reality Deviants? That sounds like a significant change in focus.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, the Nephandi's actions make a hell of a lot more sense this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, &quot;spiritual Consensus manipulation&quot; isn't an exact science... Yet (not for technocrats anyway, but I think that animistic scientists, or tech-shamans, could deal with that problema with a scientific approach).<br /> <br /> Lets not forget that Dimensional Science, actually is an extremily Paradigm limited version of the Spirit Sphere, and that the Union have many blindfolds about the spiritual realities because of their own beliefs.<br /> <br /> That being said, it is worth of note that the Union in fact DO EXACTLY that... Hell, those maniacs are trying to FORMAT THE UMBRA.<br /> <br /> The only thing is... This is an herculean effort.<br /> <br /> And still... They've managed to do it, with an outstanding level of success. How much formated space have they managed to create? Look at their crazy efforts to reinforce the Gauntlet and the Dreamshell (sorry, I don't know the name in english for the barrier with the Deep Umbra).<br /> <br /> Here, there are two possibilities:<br /> <br /> They know what they are doing. At some level, they do, in fact. It doesn't matter if they actually know that &quot;Consensus&quot; is a spirit thing, what they know is: keeping the extra dimensional things away for a day, keeps Earth safe for 1.000 days.<br /> <br /> They don't know what they are doing... But their actions show results. Fortify the Dreamshell as much as you can; those Cthulhus out there can't come here now. It doesn't matter what's causing those changes, what's matter is that IT WORKS.<br /> <br /> Besides, the actions of the reality deviants are NOT insignificant.<br /> <br /> First of all, the vast majority of Chimerical spirits will be in the Dreaming, changing THAT reality. One chimera or another may enter the material world and cause problems, but those are minor exceptions. Millions of specters dwell in the labirinth and tempest, but only some tiny few will actually possess the living. And the Malfeans are actually sleeping &quot;peacefully&quot; most of the time, and even when awake, they don't come to the material world. Wyrm Incarnas can invade and corrupt many Umbral Realms... But almost never will come to Earth.<br /> <br /> The truth is: spiritual interference on Earth is a minor thing. Yes, you do have some thousands of water spirits on a river. But, they are not possessing people or materializing, or turning houses close to it into shells. Rather, they keep only making the waters of the River flowing. The millions of earth elementals in a city, will just stay there, sleeping and keeping the soil stable. <br /> <br /> The majority of spirits are just keeping the &quot;metaphysical inertia&quot;. They aren't actively &quot;shaping reality&quot;, but rather, they are KEEPING it.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure the Union would love to vaporize all the trillions of banes out there if they could.<br /> <br /> Well... Good luck with that.<br /> <br /> Now, while the spirits will pretty much be a minor influence on the material world (in the sense that they mostly keep things as they are, instead of being a major cause for mayhem), Deviants are a real danger... Not to mention that MANY deviants will act UPON THE SPIRITS THEMSELVES. <br /> <br /> I mean... If spirits are the reality builders... How dangerous is a Dreamspeaker acting as a kind of &quot;spiritual syndicate&quot;? Or an Hermetic using &quot;slave labor&quot; to change reality?<br /> <br /> If anything, I'd say this makes the deviants even MORE dangerous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:31:46-08:00","id":1049995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049874#post1049874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps the consensus is a giant mindless spirit that is impossible to detect. Anything that shapes the consensus is within the spirits control, anything that doesn't, isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a good name for this Consensus-entity-like.<br /> <br /> The One.<br /> <br /> Yep... Spiritual Consensus could, in fact, be the real &quot;face&quot; of &quot;The One&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:50:14-08:00","id":1050003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049926#post1049926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Objection to Quantumboost 1:</b> There's a potential chain reaction here. If a being (say an Umbral representation of an omnipotent god) is believed to be more connected to things it will become so. As it does it's own ability to reflect things will grow. With no natural limit, one creature (or a few) could grow to massively dominate reality to the point that no one else gets a say.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In a hypotetical scenario where the Weaver &quot;conquers all the hearts and minds&quot; of all beings in the Tellurian, or the Wyrm... What would happen? Eternal Ecstasy or absolute Entropy? Yes or sure?<br /> <br /> And... What will happen if the Oblivion grows so much that encompass <i>almost</i> all?<br /> <br /> So, I would say... Yes. That's not really an objection, because... In fact, it could happen. In fact, at least 2 entities are actively trying to achieve EXACTLY that, under WoD lore (the Weaver and the Wyrm).<br /> <br /> And that shows just how dangerous imbalance could be for the world.<br /> <br /> And, if we consider that &quot;Universal Consensus&quot; (that is, the Consensus brought about by ALL entities in the universe) could in fact, be the entity called &quot;The One&quot; (God, The Creator, The Primordial Being, whatever), than yes, it's already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:57:55-08:00","id":1050006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049959#post1049959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not especially, because my scenario was meant to examine what would happen if people adapted an affirmative belief about the nature of subjective reality. If reality is subjective, can it be made not-subjective by sufficient belief? <br /> <br /> <b>Scenario 2</b>: A sufficient number of people to alter consensual reality believe in Des Moines, Iowa's Civic Center there exists a representation of a square circle. They do not believe any special definitions of the terms 'square' or 'circle', and believe that a square is a regular two-dimensional geometric shape with exactly four sides of equal length, and that a circle is a regular two-dimensional geometric shape with exactly one side, each point of which is equidistant from the midpoint of a line segment that bisects the shape.<br /> <br /> What do we see in the Des Moines Civic Center when we go to see the thing that is believed to exist?<br /> <br /> <b>Purpose of the Scenario</b>: Does the nature of consensual reality permit the existence of a thing with mutually exclusive attributes? A logical impossibility, if you would.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's, in fact, quite common on many Umbral landscapes... So, Im inclined to say &quot;yes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides, that example is not actually factual. You are just playing with semantics here, not real illogical things. What you would get from your example is a town full of people that call circles as &quot;squares&quot;. If people define squares as 4 sides geometrics, that's the meaning it has for them. And 1 side (or infinite sides, defending on the geometry you use) figures are not &quot;squares&quot;. It's the same thing to say &quot;if it is an undead and sucks the blood of living, it is a chair!&quot;. You are just giving the word &quot;chair&quot; a new meaning, not changing the meaning of vampires. PurePure semantics.<br /> <br /> Really illogical things: time travel is possible, and you can travel back in time and stop your past self from time travelling.<br /> <br /> Now... That would be an interesting &quot;Paradigm&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T06:28:41-08:00","id":1050460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049979#post1049979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think addressing this has to go back to a more thorough definition of Consensus. I'm aware you have good reasons to try to minimize the focus on that, but it really feels like you can't escape the necessity to get into more detail about to maintain a coherent evolution from the first principle.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this is another issue that's less with the growing principle, and more like my initial &quot;objection to approach.&quot; There's an axiomatic issue with the ill-defined nature of Consensus. That is, Consensus is an axiom of this experiment without the direct definition an axiom should have. Too an extent, we're trying to do algebra where &quot;addition/subtraction,&quot; is not well defined. Even if there's some algebra you can do without defining addition/subtraction, it gets very limited and creates an incomplete set of principles. </div> </div> </div>Had to spend a night thinking about this. I don't think we can treat the Consensus as an axiom, ill definined or otherwise; it is too important that its nature be on the table. If there are axioms here they are probably deeper terminology issues, like what do we mean when we say belief. We may need to specify what we mean, although I can't be the sole judge on that.<br /> <br /> Having said that you and Quantumboost have me dead to rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049436#post1049436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Objection to Ramnesis 3:</b> If 80% believe something (unrelated to personhood or meta-Consensus etc.), but 10% believe in something which contradicts that, and 'enough' believe in the contradictory nature of those two possibilities, then you would have the lesser-believed thing be 'possible', but the greater-believed thing being 'certain' rather than uncertain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a contradiction, and reality on the brink or not, the current definition of belief doesn't allow for that. It has to change. <br /> <br /> Now I see two ways of doing that. One is to change the percentages and the other is to change the consensus to something more complex than a strict numerical relationship. Given the spirit of the experiment I think the former is better. So how about 'If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, <i>91% and it's certain.</i>'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049979#post1049979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a broad scale? No. On a local Reality Zone scale? There are places where this could be an issue. For example there's an island in the pacific where all the current inhabitants are descended from a shipwreck's survivors. With a low genetic diversity and founder effect in play, a rare genetic eye condition (which results in a strange form of color-blindness and high levels of light sensitivity) is extremely common in this one place. So until that island reconnected with the modern world, it would have to be the case that on that island things looked fundamentally different than the same version of those things elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a resolution for this that fits the current iteration, but that I absolutely hate and would have to make my own objection to. I also have a dodge that relies on a lot of hair splitting that everyone will hate. But then I realized there was one other element we have to tackle first. Do the inhabitants have any expectations about the parts of the spectrum they can't see? Because it they don't they aren't really stopping (and wouldn't even notice) the trees from matching the expectations of people who could see those parts of the spectrum. Basically, does color even exist if there is no one around to see it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the premise of a subjective reality I'm uncertain as to the difference between Metaphysical Inertia and Expectation Inertia. Expectations only have inertia in this context because of the metaphysics involved. </div> </div> </div>Well there are things in Mage, like Mythic Threads, that have disproportional inertia. As of yet they aren't incorporated into my model, but they may be at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Objection to Ramnesis 4</b>: How does equal potential impact on Consensus logically flow with unequal strength of individual beliefs? If equality of impact is a fundamental aspect of Consensus, then beliefs can only be as strong as the weight of belief in them. There's no mechanism for a belief to gain strength in excess of net balance of extant beliefs by all applicable persons. </div> </div> </div>I was speaking more on an individual level. If I have never been near a fire before, only seen one from a distance, I might have a strong belief that fire is bright but little belief about its temperature.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Ramnesis 5</b>: Reality is almost completely malleable. If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, <i>91% and it's certain.</i>Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating. The Conensus cannot change who affects it or change anyone's personhood, or change their mental or spiritual state.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:42:30-08:00","id":1050520,"title":"","content":"How does this effect Bygones? Bygones can be sapient, so are they people? Or is your definition of person restricted to humans? If so, how human do you have to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:04:48-08:00","id":1050596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1050460#post1050460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we can treat the Consensus as an axiom, ill definined or otherwise; it is too important that its nature be on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case, a starting definition of Consensus itself (rather than the current efforts to refine how it works) is still essential to how we're approaching this. Defining Consensus directly seems like it should be part of the first principle along with reality being subjective and mutable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I see two ways of doing that. One is to change the percentages and the other is to change the consensus to something more complex than a strict numerical relationship. Given the spirit of the experiment I think the former is better. So how about 'If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, <i>91% and it's certain.</i>' </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about the spirit of things here. Why is assigning arbitrary numbers and then adjusting them to avoid a specific paradoxical result more to the spirit of this exercise than considering a different approach to how to define the effect of massing belief towards the actualization of that belief.<br /> <br /> To take the point a bit further: humans have well demonstrated the ability to hold mutually contradictory beliefs. Belief is not - at least for humans - a zero-sum game. The numbers solution only works if all persons involved never hold contradictory beliefs. With humans it is distinctly possible to have a belief that has &gt;10% belief and &gt;91% contradictory belief in the same population.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, while the numeric abstraction is functional to a point, it doesn't hold up to continued expansion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, does color even exist if there is no one around to see it? </div> </div> </div>That's sort of the question I was posing to you in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well there are things in Mage, like Mythic Threads, that have disproportional inertia. As of yet they aren't incorporated into my model, but they may be at some point. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how this explains the difference between metaphysical and expectational inertia in this context. I'm also not sure we can qualify Mythic Threads as &quot;disproportional&quot; in this regard. What are they out of proportion with? The whole point of them is that these beliefs have inertia even if there's a certain amount of acknowledgement of them as &quot;myths.&quot; This can even apply to modern myths/urban legends. Physics says that bullets don't have enough power to knock a human backwards significantly, but I can pull on the Thread of the pop-action myth to add Forces to a Firearms attack to knock someone back. My ability to do so is proportional to the power that myth has in pop culture, right? I mean we can actually demonstrate this in real life to an extent. In cultures that watch a lot of action movies, gunshot victims tend to act more injured (in line with action movie tropes) than they actually are, while in cultures without such pop-myths that see gun violence only in reality react as the injury itself would dictate biologically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T11:15:47-08:00","id":1050603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1050596#post1050596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how this explains the difference between metaphysical and expectational inertia in this context. I'm also not sure we can qualify Mythic Threads as &amp;quot;disproportional&amp;quot; in this regard. What are they out of proportion with? The whole point of them is that these beliefs have inertia even if there's a certain amount of acknowledgement of them as &amp;quot;myths.&amp;quot; This can even apply to modern myths/urban legends. Physics says that bullets don't have enough power to knock a human backwards significantly, but I can pull on the Thread of the pop-action myth to add Forces to a Firearms attack to knock someone back. My ability to do so is proportional to the power that myth has in pop culture, right? I mean we can actually demonstrate this in real life to an extent. In cultures that watch a lot of action movies, gunshot victims tend to act more injured (in line with action movie tropes) than they actually are, while in cultures without such pop-myths that see gun violence only in reality react as the injury itself would dictate biologically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, great point. Could we say that in a city like Hollywood, if I shoot somebody people will ACTUALLY get a kick from the shoot because that's the local Consensus? That's a great aesthetical effect to the scenario","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:00:38-08:00","id":1050633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wow, great point. Could we say that in a city like Hollywood, if I shoot somebody people will ACTUALLY get a kick from the shoot because that's the local Consensus? That's a great aesthetical effect to the scenario </div> </div> </div>That would be quite interesting, what will the forensic departament say to explain this to people form other places? : &quot;Oh, the bullet didn't kill him, it was te contusion caused when he flew backwards...What, that bullets can't knock a human backward significantly?...Oh, you don't know that because you're foreigner, it's because it's hollywood, guns don't work the same here&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:04:41-08:00","id":1050635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1050633#post1050633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be quite interesting, what will the forensic departament say to explain this to people form other places? : &amp;quot;Oh, the bullet didn't kill him, it was te contusion caused when he flew backwards...What, that bullets can't knock a human backward significantly?...Oh, you don't know that because you're foreigner, it's because it's hollywood, guns don't work the same here&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And enters the NWO agent with the mind eraser...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:22:46-08:00","id":1050650,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm sure he's falling from the sky right now, while cursing the Syndicate for insisting in making movies that contradict reality.<br /> <br /> In fact, theres an entire Construct of the NWO that exists solely with the purposse of tackling &quot;movie related deviations&quot; in Holliwood, like when someone discovers that everything it's more flammable and prone to explode, but that the expansive wave of explosions don't reach as far and being near won't cause deafness. Or when someone punches a guy, sending him through a wall without causing much damage to the victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T12:23:13-08:00","id":1050651,"title":"","content":"I would actually argue that in a place like Hollywood pop-culture tropes are <b>less</b> potent towards any local Reality Zones because there's so many people there that know how fake it all is. When you have a huge industry there that's all about people faking it entertainingly, they're likely to be much more conscious of it being fake than buy it as plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T15:31:26-08:00","id":1050763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1050651#post1050651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually argue that in a place like Hollywood pop-culture tropes are <b>less</b> potent towards any local Reality Zones because there's so many people there that know how fake it all is. When you have a huge industry there that's all about people faking it entertainingly, they're likely to be much more conscious of it being fake than buy it as plausible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means you might be able to get away with doing way more coincidental magic. Big fireball explosion? Someone at Special Effects no doubt. You have claws and horns? Prosthetics are getting really good these days. Did that bus just float? That must be a sophisticated rig you've got there, I didn't even see the strings!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T17:14:58-08:00","id":1050807,"title":"","content":"Except, again, you have far more people in the area that know what that actually takes. The average person living it Hollywood is going to be more skeptical of a big fireball because they're used to all the things studios do when setting those off in public. You don't film big explosions in downtown LA without a lot of things happening to make sure the public doesn't get hurt or think it's real. You don't walk around with claws and horns, because those good effects takes ~4-6 hours to achieve, and you don't do that just to stroll around town, you have to get on set and work because you only have a few hours before the sweat starts to undo even the best stuff without touch ups (and none of them work as real weapons). Buses don't float without rigging, there's lots of tricks but they only work live from the angle of the camera, not from the general observer.<br /> <br /> Again, the more people you have around that do this stuff for a living because it's a major industry in the city, the more people that aren't going to be easily distracted by Blatancy style bluffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T05:47:44-08:00","id":1051958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1050596#post1050596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, a starting definition of Consensus itself (rather than the current efforts to refine how it works) is still essential to how we're approaching this. Defining Consensus directly seems like it should be part of the first principle along with reality being subjective and mutable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable. Would a simple: &quot;The Consensus is the sum of all belief and expectation&quot; work as a starting point? I don't think distance or weight need to be in the definition as we area already working on those, but is there something else I am missing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not so sure about the spirit of things here. Why is assigning arbitrary numbers and then adjusting them to avoid a specific paradoxical result more to the spirit of this exercise than considering a different approach to how to define the effect of massing belief towards the actualization of that belief. </div> </div> </div>Because how the mathematical model breaks down is important for figuring out the next iteration. Just knowing that the maths can conflict doesn't mean they always do, nor does it tell you anything about why. I mean, look at what you just proposed:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To take the point a bit further: humans have well demonstrated the ability to hold mutually contradictory beliefs. Belief is not - at least for humans - a zero-sum game. The numbers solution only works if all persons involved never hold contradictory beliefs. With humans it is distinctly possible to have a belief that has &gt;10% belief and &gt;91% contradictory belief in the same population. </div> </div> </div>I'm trying my hardest (though not always succeeding) to not anticipate future complaints, so I wouldn't have written the next iteration to tackle the issue contradictory beliefs, that would have had to wait till it came up on other fronts. More importantly, that isn't the way I would have chosen to knock down the mathematical model. I would have focused on that grey area where things are probable but not certain. So if I had anticipated I would have only dealt with part of the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's sort of the question I was posing to you in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Here's something we need to figure out before I can deal with your objection (as well as BenjCano's): What happens when the contradiction is completely out of sight? In cases like this (or Schodinger's Cat) when an observer can't tell the difference between this strange model and the real world, is there a problem?<br /> <br /> What about contradictions whose practical effects match oddities we see in the real world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure how this explains the difference between metaphysical and expectational inertia in this context. I'm also not sure we can qualify Mythic Threads as &quot;disproportional&quot; in this regard. What are they out of proportion with? The whole point of them is that these beliefs have inertia even if there's a certain amount of acknowledgement of them as &quot;myths.&quot; This can even apply to modern myths/urban legends. Physics says that bullets don't have enough power to knock a human backwards significantly, but I can pull on the Thread of the pop-action myth to add Forces to a Firearms attack to knock someone back. My ability to do so is proportional to the power that myth has in pop culture, right? I mean we can actually demonstrate this in real life to an extent. In cultures that watch a lot of action movies, gunshot victims tend to act more injured (in line with action movie tropes) than they actually are, while in cultures without such pop-myths that see gun violence only in reality react as the injury itself would dictate biologically. </div> </div> </div>You know, Mythic Threads always did seem disproportional to me, but I've got to admit you are convincing me otherwise. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:50:42-08:00","id":1052056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1051958#post1051958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's reasonable. Would a simple: &quot;The Consensus is the sum of all belief and expectation&quot; work as a starting point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the sense of a first principle, yes, but there's already a number of objections that have been stated in thread that need to be address in revisions of the starting point at this juncture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because how the mathematical model breaks down is important for figuring out the next iteration. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that address the fundamental question of whether the mathematical model is the best model to use. As the mathematical model grows increasingly complex, the question of if it remains the most parsimonious model for this gains in validity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's something we need to figure out before I can deal with your objection (as well as BenjCano's): What happens when the contradiction is completely out of sight? In cases like this (or Schodinger's Cat) when an observer can't tell the difference between this strange model and the real world, is there a problem? </div> </div> </div>First off, let's keep the cat out of this. I know that it's popular, but remember that the cat is a joke about how collapsing quantum wave functions does not apply above the quantum scale. Schrodinger's whole point was that the cat is either alive or dead because cats aren't quantum scale phenomena and the life of the cat is not dependent on the observer in real world physics; just because you don't know which state the cat is in yet doesn't mean it's both.<br /> <br /> Second, we haven't established what happens during any sort of contradiction, we've just established a model that allows contradictions to occur.<br /> <br /> As it stands, it is impossible to have a contradiction without observation, because all contradictions so far are the product of conflict beliefs. Until the principle is further refined into how reality manifests contradictions so that the can exist externally to persons, we can't really say how that plays out.<br /> <br /> As to &quot;is there a problem?&quot; I'm not sure where the problem is. If the problem is in working out the principle, than yes, there's still a problem because the principle isn't sufficiently advanced to model any of this yet. If the problem is just in the &quot;do unobserved contradictions cause a problem with the goal of a universe superficially the same as our own modern world,&quot; then no, those aren't problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about contradictions whose practical effects match oddities we see in the real world? </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:14:54-08:00","id":1052097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052056#post1052056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in the sense of a first principle, yes, but there's already a number of objections that have been stated in thread that need to be address in revisions of the starting point at this juncture.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I put this in it is going to read &quot;Reality is almost completely malleable but consensus, which is the sum of all belief and expectation. If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, 91% and it's certain<i>.</i>Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that address the fundamental question of whether the mathematical model is the best model to use. As the mathematical model grows increasingly complex, the question of if it remains the most parsimonious model for this gains in validity. </div> </div> </div>I'm not planning on robustly testing every permutation, but the issue of contradictory beliefs doesn't go away just because we drop the math. I'm going to have to tackle that head on,<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First off, let's keep the cat out of this. I know that it's popular, but remember that the cat is a joke about how collapsing quantum wave functions does not apply above the quantum scale. Schrodinger's whole point was that the cat is either alive or dead because cats aren't quantum scale phenomena and the life of the cat is not dependent on the observer in real world physics; just because you don't know which state the cat is in yet doesn't mean it's both. </div> </div> </div>I'm well aware it's been massively understood, that's actually why I brought it up. Because his example was misunderstood a significant chunk of the population (possibly even the majority of people who are aware of it) think something can be in two states at once (so long as we don't see it). If real world people are okay with that actually happening, how do we view it as an impossibility in our model? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, we haven't established what happens during any sort of contradiction, we've just established a model that allows contradictions to occur.<br /> <br /> As it stands, it is impossible to have a contradiction without observation, because all contradictions so far are the product of conflict beliefs. Until the principle is further refined into how reality manifests contradictions so that the can exist externally to persons, we can't really say how that plays out. </div> </div> </div>If it were possible, I'd love to test if a reality that only exists when seen actually functions. Considering spirits count as observers I don't think that's possible. Another time, perhaps.<br /> <br /> As to &quot;is there a problem?&quot; I'm not sure where the problem is. If the problem is in working out the principle, than yes, there's still a problem because the principle isn't sufficiently advanced to model any of this yet. If the problem is just in the &quot;do unobserved contradictions cause a problem with the goal of a universe superficially the same as our own modern world,&quot; then no, those aren't problems.[/quote]<br /> <br /> The latter was my thinking. It's pretty clear it is time to change the principle, I'm just trying to figure out the easiest way to cover the objections so far, and I wanted to make sure I wasn't being arbitrary. I'll try to have a new revision up tomorrow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you give an example? </div> </div> </div>I brought up the Blue/White Dress incident in response to BenjCano's objection earlier. Yes, it's obviously an optical illusion, but if the dress were actually blue to some people and white to others, it would present almost exactly the same way. This kind of thing couldn't happen every day, but my intuition is that strange one-time incidents don't invalidate my model world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:55:44-08:00","id":1052126,"title":"","content":"I think the solution for contraditory Consensus would be a <b>Reality Dissonance</b> (as opposed to real world cognitive dissonance, where a person can have contraditory beliefs)<br /> <br /> Actually, I propose that the scenario of MAGE already has exactly that. Each Umbral zone, Realm, etc, are actually <i>dissonant realities</i>, for all purposes. Hell, the material (real?) world is a reality dissonant from the many Umbras. Another thing that can give weight to that theory: all the different Reality Zones, they are all Dissonant Realities (and all that is a proof that there is no single, unified reality, or Consensus. So, I keep the firm belief that Umbral realities are based on different LOCAL Consensus - and <i>local</i> is the key world here)<br /> <br /> For further ways to look at it, this discussions (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...rder-of-reason</a>) would ilustrate that point.<br /> <br /> Was Earth flat before the Order of Reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:02:34-08:00","id":1052129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052097#post1052097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought up the Blue/White Dress incident in response to BenjCano's objection earlier. Yes, it's obviously an optical illusion, but if the dress were actually blue to some people and white to others, it would present almost exactly the same way. This kind of thing couldn't happen every day, but my intuition is that strange one-time incidents don't invalidate my model world.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040063#post1040063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Earth existed in a state of quantum flux in which it was flat, round, spherical, an oblate spheroid, cube-shaped, stacked on the back of a turtle, or floating in a blob of god-sperm simultaneously/none of the above until an observer believed in it hard enough and collapsed the quantum wave state for the duration of the observation.</div> </div> </div> </div>THAT'S more or less how a &quot;Quantum Reality Dissonance&quot; would play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:09:41-08:00","id":1052138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040029-was-earth-flat-before-the-order-of-reason?p=1040084#post1040084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the Earth was flat for many people, but round for Pythagoras and the poliniseans.<br /> <br /> Those that believed Earth was flat, would drop from its edge, directly to some Umbra (into the Low Umbra perhaps?). Pythagoras and the poliniseans, would travel across the Atlantic, and instead of seeing the Edge of the world, would see the other &amp;quot;side&amp;quot; of Earth, on the Pacific, and would apear in the &amp;quot;other end&amp;quot; of the world's &amp;quot;disc&amp;quot;. Space is an illusion, after all.<br /> <br /> Andd those believing in giant turtles and eelephants, would see a turtle with the size of J\u00fapiter with 3 elephants on top of each the size of Uranus holding a flat Earth on their backs, as they fell in the primordial Umbral Sea...<br /> <br /> How would Pythagoras disappear from the Atlanttic and reach the Pac\u00edfic? Space connections between those seas, only acesdible by those that believe it so.<br /> <br /> About the Americas, it wouldn't be an EPHEMERAL world in the Umbra... Hell, the separation between matter and spirit is a recent event. At that time, its higly possible that &amp;quot;other Earths&amp;quot; existed... Actually, at least each continent were, in fact, A DIFFERENT world. Why didn't no one &amp;quot;discovered&amp;quot; the Australia before? Probably, because it were a separeted world. In such scenarios, the explorations of the VE made a lot more sense. And, it's even possible that some other worlds were left behind by our Earth... Maybe the Hollow Earth co</div> </div> </div> </div>And also that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:51:41-08:00","id":1052301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052097#post1052097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not planning on robustly testing every permutation, but the issue of contradictory beliefs doesn't go away just because we drop the math. I'm going to have to tackle that head on,</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously we can't test every permutation, but we can narrow the options to a few others instead of doggedly sticking to one, right?<br /> <br /> And yes, contradictory beliefs don't go away, but a more qualitative approach might have an easier time with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If real world people are okay with that actually happening, how do we view it as an impossibility in our model? </div> </div> </div>I not sure I buy the premise of the question. I don't think most people actually believe in the misunderstood cat. It's just a short hand they use to talk about something on a basic level. There's a difference between knowing about the idea of something, and believing it. I would argue that most people being told that there's a cat in a box, belief the cat is either alive or dead, not in a state of both.<br /> <br /> The cat might become some sort of quirky Mythic Thread (how useful could that be...) but not strong enough to actually be &quot;real.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it were possible, I'd love to test if a reality that only exists when seen actually functions. Considering spirits count as observers I don't think that's possible. Another time, perhaps. </div> </div> </div>I find George Berkeley's writings on what would later called subjective idealism fairly useful in a philosophic testing of this concept.<br /> <br /> He's a bit biased, in that his argument is ultimately that the &quot;spirits count as observers&quot; issue is his proof that an omniscient observer deity must exist because reality is consistent. But his discussions of why that must be the case do involve a lot of exploration of what a reality where only perception counts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I brought up the Blue/White Dress incident in response to BenjCano's objection earlier. Yes, it's obviously an optical illusion, but if the dress were actually blue to some people and white to others, it would present almost exactly the same way. This kind of thing couldn't happen every day, but my intuition is that strange one-time incidents don't invalidate my model world. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I must have forgotten about that.<br /> <br /> I think this gets into an odd point of perceptions vs beliefs. While we frequently have surface beliefs informed by perceptions, those are also largely fleeting. An optical illusion isn't something I would consider a belief. I guess I'm looking for something a bit more robust in terms of having strongly shaped beliefs or expectations being at odds with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T20:15:27-08:00","id":1052363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052301#post1052301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, I must have forgotten about that.<br /> <br /> I think this gets into an odd point of perceptions vs beliefs. While we frequently have surface beliefs informed by perceptions, those are also largely fleeting. An optical illusion isn't something I would consider a belief. I guess I'm looking for something a bit more robust in terms of having strongly shaped beliefs or expectations being at odds with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>People have many cognitive dissonances; that's a basic thing on religious thinking, and the core concept behind the idea of the &quot;doublethinking&quot; of the book 1984. That book is also a great souce for the idea of &quot;Consensual reality&quot; (I find it fascinating when the villain say &quot;if I wanted, I could fly, right here. We create truth; if the party says, it not only it is true, but it simply is the way that it has always been - and no one would question it. Oh, that's soooo technocratic, it get me a boner everytime my instructor in the NWO would read us this... I could see with my open eyes myself saying these to some deviant terrorist...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T05:56:19-08:00","id":1052523,"title":"","content":"So what I'm seeing right now are a couple of significant problems involving contradictions. There's the issue of the same person holding two mutually exclusive beliefs. There is issue of a nigh certainties being in competition with distinct possibilities. There is the issue of drift outside of observation. And there is the issue of very visible strange behavior when half the population says one thing and half of it says another.<br /> <br /> A lot of this can be handled by introducing some kind of principle of consistency, such that strange behavior either happens rarely enough to be ignored or consistently enough to look normal. That's yet another exception to the current model that belief <i>is</i> reality, so I'm going to propose instead a belief <i>makes</i> reality. That means that once reality is in existence it doesn't need belief to continue, but will solidify and erode in the presence of confirming or contradicting beliefs respectively. This still means a lot of strange things can happen, but existing reality still has a say in outright contradictions.<br /> <br /> If it helps, my mental model is a freezing sea filled with icebergs of solidified reality. Belief builds up or melts down reality to fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Ramnesis 6</b>: Reality was created by belief and is almost completely malleable to the sum of all belief and expectation. Belief and expectation strengthen acceptable parts of reality and erode unacceptable parts. The shape reality is pushed towards is known as the Consensus. Things are possible if reality permits/demands they happen or is too weak to stop them. Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating. Nothing can change who affects reality or change anyone's personhood, or their mental or spiritual state.<br /> <br /> How's that for a substantial change?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:06:36-08:00","id":1052760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052523#post1052523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...That's yet another exception to the current model that belief <i>is</i> reality, so I'm going to propose instead a belief <i>makes</i> reality. That means that once reality is in existence it doesn't need belief to continue, but will solidify and erode in the presence of confirming or contradicting beliefs respectively. This still means a lot of strange things can happen, but existing reality still has a say in outright contradictions.<br /> <br /> If it helps, my mental model is a freezing sea filled with icebergs of solidified reality. Belief builds up or melts down reality to fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that's the most perfect analogy... Belief makes reality, and after that it becames inertial, until eroded<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052523#post1052523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<b>Ramnesis 6</b>: Reality was created by belief and is almost completely malleable to the sum of all belief and expectation. Belief and expectation strengthen acceptable parts of reality and erode unacceptable parts. The shape reality is pushed towards is known as the Consensus. Things are possible if reality permits/demands they happen or is too weak to stop them. Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating. Nothing can change who affects reality or change anyone's personhood, or their mental or spiritual state.<br /> <br /> How's that for a substantial change?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can call it a day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:17:36-08:00","id":1052768,"title":"","content":"I think it's going well (consider the nature of my current critiques a good sign for how this seems to be going). That said!<br /> <br /> <b>Objections to Ramnesis 6</b>:<br /> <br /> The statement of &quot;reality was created by belief,&quot; is problematic. It opens a huge box that seems unnecessary. It's like trying to claim that evolution explains the origin of life, when evolution is based on a presumption of life existing with no statement on how it started. This should be rephrased to, &quot;The current state of reality is created by belief...&quot; to avoid complicating the presumptive nature of a subjective reality &quot;starting&quot; somehow. How reality started doesn't matter, only how reality is at any given moment and how it will be taking account the effect of previous moments matters.<br /> <br /> &quot;Acceptable&quot; seems a questionable semantic choice. It implies a judgement without any source to be making this judgement. What if this was something more like, &quot;Belief and expectation create and strength coherent parts of reality, and erode incoherent parts.&quot; This sets up a lot of the other sections. Strong beliefs are more effective because of their coherence (this applies to Consensus and to things like a mage's Focus and why some paradigms aren't successful: they're incoherent and incapable of a strong impact on reality). Entrenched ideas are empowered because they set up a chain reaction of coherence compared to other options; emergent patterns happen because coherence makes for stronger beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T16:15:19-08:00","id":1052879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052768#post1052768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Objections to Ramnesis 6</b>:<br /> <br /> The statement of &quot;reality was created by belief&quot; is problematic. It opens a huge box that seems unnecessary. It's like trying to claim that evolution explains the origin of life, when evolution is based on a presumption of life existing with no statement on how it started. This should be rephrased to, &quot;The current state of reality is created by belief...&quot; to avoid complicating the presumptive nature of a subjective reality &quot;starting&quot; somehow. How reality started doesn't matter, only how reality is at any given moment and how it will be taking account the effect of previous moments matters.<br /> <br /> &quot;Acceptable&quot; seems a questionable semantic choice. It implies a judgement without any source to be making this judgement. What if this was something more like, &quot;Belief and expectation create and strength coherent parts of reality, and erode incoherent parts.&amp;quo64 This sets up a lot of the other sections. Strong beliefs are more effective because of their coherence (this applies to Consensus and to things like a mage's Focus and why some paradigms aren't successful: they're incoherent and incapable of a strong impact on reality). Entrenched ideas are empowered because they set up a chain reaction of coherence compared to other options; emergent patterns happen because coherence makes for stronger beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a min","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T09:18:59-08:00","id":1053259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1052768#post1052768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's going well (consider the nature of my current critiques a good sign for how this seems to be going). That said!</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Objections to Ramnesis 6</b>:<br /> <br /> The statement of &quot;reality was created by belief,&quot; is problematic. It opens a huge box that seems unnecessary. It's like trying to claim that evolution explains the origin of life, when evolution is based on a presumption of life existing with no statement on how it started. This should be rephrased to, &quot;The current state of reality is created by belief...&quot; to avoid complicating the presumptive nature of a subjective reality &quot;starting&quot; somehow. How reality started doesn't matter, only how reality is at any given moment and how it will be taking account the effect of previous moments matters. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree, that was an unnecessary specification. I'm not even interested in taking a stand on if subjective reality did start or if it's always been that way. Your wording works for keeping both options open.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Acceptable&quot; seems a questionable semantic choice. It implies a judgement without any source to be making this judgement. What if this was something more like, &quot;Belief and expectation create and strength coherent parts of reality, and erode incoherent parts.&quot; This sets up a lot of the other sections. Strong beliefs are more effective because of their coherence (this applies to Consensus and to things like a mage's Focus and why some paradigms aren't successful: they're incoherent and incapable of a strong impact on reality). Entrenched ideas are empowered because they set up a chain reaction of coherence compared to other options; emergent patterns happen because coherence makes for stronger beliefs. </div> </div> </div>I agree that 'acceptable' is probably the wrong term, but I think 'coherent' is as well. The intention of this model is that the force of belief is what shapes reality. I do agree that coherent ideas will tend to be the strongest and have the most impact because they reinforce themselves and others, but I see that as an emergent element of the system. So I think the term we may be looking for here is 'conforming.'<br /> <br /> <b>Ramnesis 7</b>: <i>The current state of reality</i> is created by belief and is almost completely malleable to the sum of all belief and expectation. Belief and expectation strengthen <i>conforming</i> parts of reality and erode <i>nonconforming</i> parts. The shape reality is pushed towards is known as the Consensus. Things are possible if reality permits/demands they happen or is too weak to stop them. Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating. Nothing can change who affects reality or change anyone's personhood, or their mental or spiritual state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 02-22-2017, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:50:47-08:00","id":1053926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049502#post1049502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, if you assume that the belief of spirits are capable of shaping reality, then the differences between Objective Reality and Subjective Reality are academic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It lends some level of inertia to things - the entity's belief in itself resists others' beliefs about it, but that doesn't require it to resist outside influences <i>absolutely and incontrovertibly</i>. The 'spirit of a rock' is just that rock's belief in its own existence and properties, and that can be eroded with the proper outside influences.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just out of curiosity, where does it say in Mage that the sleeping Avatar is the mechanism by which human belief shapes the Consensus? And Jagglings are presented as being as sapient. </div> </div> </div>That's more definitional, imo. &quot;Avatar&quot; is essentially a term in Traditions lingo that means &quot;that thing what we have that lets us do magick&quot;. So a &quot;sleeping Avatar&quot; is just... an acknowledgement of Consensus's existence and relationship with Sleepers.<br /> <br /> For Jagglings, well, we're discussing a hypothetical model of how a Consensual Reality <i>could</i> work so Jagglings being presented as sapient is just a question of (a) how much of that needs to be kept and (b) how much of that is a Chinese Room issue, where they <i>seem</i> sapient because people expect them to behave in an anthropomorphised way and hence see them that way, but don't necessarily believe they're actually us-like enough to actually <i>be</i> sapient?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049926#post1049926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Objection to Quantumboost 1:</b> There's a potential chain reaction here. If a being (say an Umbral representation of an omnipotent god) is believed to be more connected to things it will become so. As it does it's own ability to reflect things will grow. With no natural limit, one creature (or a few) could grow to massively dominate reality to the point that no one else gets a say.</div> </div> </div> </div>That imposes a constraint on how much 'belief in entity X' can increase its powers, yes. Given a non-degenerate weighting curve, that seems fine; if <i>actually everybody</i> believes that Thing X represents the totality of truth about the universe, or enough do that it becomes a self-reinforcing phenomenon... well, that's just winning the Ascension War for your paradigm, isn't it? I'd think that's desirable; if nothing else as a Technocratic Victory for the Technos to strive for and the Traditions to oppose, rather than everything being pointless unwinnable/unlosable futility.<br /> <br /> If not everybody believes it, that can still be eroded so long as no single entity can outweigh all other human-scale entities, which shouldn't happen if those human-scale entities can contemplate the topic at all or there are <i>very few</i> of them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1050460#post1050460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a contradiction, and reality on the brink or not, the current definition of belief doesn't allow for that. It has to change.<br /> <br /> Now I see two ways of doing that. One is to change the percentages and the other is to change the consensus to something more complex than a strict numerical relationship. Given the spirit of the experiment I think the former is better. So how about 'If you can get 10% of the local people to believe something it is possible, 66% and it's likely, <i>91% and it's certain.</i>'</div> </div> </div> </div>Numerically speaking, all you <i>really</i> need are decent breakpoints (which should be set <i>after</i> we've determined how things ought to work more generally, not before). I'd say that &quot;monotonically increasing with the belief in that result and monotonically decreasing with respect to the disbelief&quot; is a good guideline, since otherwise adding belief or removing disbelief goes backwards from what it should. It should also not make something outright impossible prior to hitting 0% belief (so that a lone Willworker can do something truly Vulgar) or outright guaranteed before 100% (so... well, the same, and to have self-consistency at least as long as people believe in self-consistency.<br /> <br /> Numericizing before you've even got to the point of figuring out what something should <i>do</i> is premature optimization, which is the root of all evils.<br /> <br /> Though it looks like you've moved past that, so good show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 02-23-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T15:53:21-08:00","id":1054057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1053259#post1053259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ramnesis 7</b>: <i>The current state of reality</i> is created by belief and is almost completely malleable to the sum of all belief and expectation. Belief and expectation strengthen <i>conforming</i> parts of reality and erode <i>nonconforming</i> parts. The shape reality is pushed towards is known as the Consensus. Things are possible if reality permits/demands they happen or is too weak to stop them. Everyone has the same potential impact on the Consensus, though some beliefs are stronger than others. At some point in the past, certain basic ideas like physical interaction and gravity were entrenched in the Consensus, these are largely self perpetuating. Nothing can change who affects reality or change anyone's personhood, or their mental or spiritual state.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there's always more extrapolation we could do, this seems to me to hold up as the coherent explanation of subjective reality to achieve the goal of the setting of Mage being a possible outcome of this expanded principle. I can't come up with anything that wouldn't amount to minor quibbling that's pointless in comparison to the contradictions without the different books of the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T19:12:48-08:00","id":1054149,"title":"","content":"I guess this small experience is a total success, at least for those that like the idea of a subjective reality; it explains most of the scenario, without random arbitrary &quot;laws&quot; that dictate some things are beyond reach, others fair game, without any good reasons. It even gives an <i>appareance</i> of objective reality (like Aya said, this subtle difference would become something much more academic than actually visible at the naked eye, althouth the consequences of such a difference are VERY deep). And, one could use the idea of &quot;local spiritual Consensus&quot; to try to bind toghether all the splats that, on MANY situations, contradict each other violently. And now, we have a very fluid scenario, were nothing is arbitrary; actually, everything, every small little piece of this reality, have a reason, and is in harmony. Hell, the ST could even change absurd things without making the scenario utterly absurd - so, all of the suddenly, old extinct Atlantida could've had floating Islands like the movie &quot;Avatar&quot; functioning under principles of &quot;anti-gravitons&quot;, or as a (more lame solution) deal with gravity spirits to &quot;change local Consensus&quot;, and that WOULDN'T break the scenario or be absurd - without the whole &quot;Earthly Foundations can't be changed, but <i>bend</i> a little - or similar random nonsense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T05:51:32-08:00","id":1054277,"title":"","content":"I'm very pleased with where this ended up. I think it successfully shows that there aren't a lot of limitations you have to place on subjective reality before it is stable enough to game in. While I can think of questions to ask, they don't change much about what the modern setting looks like.<br /> <br /> Some of the more interesting takeaways of this model:<br /> <br /> The collective weight of belief, reality, and the Consensus are three separate yet related things. <br /> <br /> I was expecting to have to bar spirits and supernatural creatures from impacting the Consensus. I've always thought of Mage as a human-centric game. Instead, they end up keeping the system relatively stable. <br /> <br /> There's no mention of Avatars. They can still exist for Mages, of course, but because we didn't exclude spirits from impacting the Consensus, we didn't need to appeal to any kind of special soul or sleeping Avatar to explain how humans were special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:40:49-08:00","id":1055286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1049285-working-from-first-principles-subjective-reality?p=1049529#post1049529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Scenario given R1: </b>Suppose the critical number of people were persuaded to believe that reality was not completely malleable. Would reality adapt to this belief?<br /> <b>If Yes: </b>If reality ceased being malleable, then it could not be changed later and this R1 would not be true any longer. Thus later reversions to the belief that reality was malleable would not change reality back to being malleable, since the initial changed belief would be for an unmalleable reality. Reality cannot be made completely unmalleable, therefore it is not completely malleable, and thus R1 is not true.<br /> <b>If No:</b> Then R1 is not true.<br /> <br /> \u2234 R1 cannot be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes that, at some point in the past, people stopped believing in a malleable reality. You would be surprised at how many people actually believe in a malleable reality on some level, though perhaps not the level that a Mage does.<br /> <br /> Very few people actually instinctively grok the idea of a limited hard reality that's secrets need to be uncovered, rather than simply considering science to conjure up new inventions out of the ether<br /> <br /> Therefor, R1 could be true, but that could also be changed.<br /> <br /> Which is in fact the Technocracies goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}